{"body":"Part of #1

## Question

What verification and acceptance contract is sufficient to hand off the private mobile-first MVP with confidence?

Decide the required automated and manual coverage for time-first capture, durable Save-then-enrich behavior, correction and confirmed deletion, Recent Sightings, visit-planner windowing and relative signals, empty and error states, mobile accessibility, migration/startup behavior, and the explicit exclusion of the deferred historical grid. The answer is a risk-proportionate acceptance contract, not test implementation.
","comments":[],"title":"Define MVP verification and acceptance coverage","url":"https://github.com/chris-tse/costco-chicken-tracker/issues/8"}
{"body":"Part of #1

## Question

In what implementation sequence should the repository be transformed from the superseded multi-user/location product into the resolved private capture-and-planning MVP?

Produce a handoff-ready sequence covering removal of authentication, users, stores, and admin surfaces; schema and migration reset; sighting persistence; Capture, completion, correction, and Recent Sightings; the minimal visit planner; deployment integration; verification; and reconciliation of the PRD, feature plans, context, and decision documentation. Make dependencies and independently shippable checkpoints explicit. The answer is the implementation route, not the implementation itself.
","title":"Sequence the private core-loop rebuild","url":"https://github.com/chris-tse/costco-chicken-tracker/issues/9"}
